{#
 # A form on a page of its own: one column, capped at a reading measure so the fields do not stretch
 # across the whole content area.
 #
 # This is the one page shape the app repeats — the twenty `new`/`edit` templates, byte for byte —
 # so it is named once here. It absorbs `app-measure`, which was the most repeated class left in the
 # templates.
 #
 # A component rather than a layout template, for two reasons. The twenty pages extend three
 # different bases — `admin/base` (14), `base` (4), `logbook_entry/base` (2) — and Twig has a single
 # inheritance, so a layout would have to exist once per base. The logbook one is not even fixed at
 # compile time: it picks its shell from `is_granted('ROLE_LOGBOOK_USER')`. And sitting inside the
 # page's own `body` block, this is one level from its slot and never meets the `outerBlocks` ceiling
 # that keeps `profile/base` and `sport_profile/base` on a hand-written `card-body`.
 #
 # `profile/edit` is deliberately not a call site: `profile/base` already puts its `main` block in a
 # card, so a second one would nest.
 #
 # Neither are `admin/user/new` and `admin/user/edit`, for the opposite reason: they are not one
 # column but a grid of cards — member, address, two legal guardians — and the measure below is what
 # decides how much room that grid has. Capped at 48rem each half came out at 336px, where a `col-md-4`
 # inside it is 112px: « Type de voie » wrapped onto two lines above a select too narrow to show a
 # word of its own placeholder. Nothing is wrong with the measure; a two-column form is simply not the
 # shape it measures. They take a plain `Card` at the content width instead.
 #
 # The body is captured first: a component body made of nothing but blocks is handed straight to the
 # inner component, so a `{% block content %}` written inside `<twig:Card:Body>` would become *its*
 # content block and then resolve to itself.
 #}
{% set body %}
    {% block content %}{% endblock %}
{% endset %}

<twig:Card elevated class="app-measure" {{ ...attributes }}>
    <twig:Card:Body>
        {{ body }}
    </twig:Card:Body>
</twig:Card>
